cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Corvus in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Corvus: an AI assistant for thesis supervisors"
abstract: >-
  A web application that helps thesis supervisors follow students from topic to
  defence, with predefined AI actions (trial and final reviews, chapter feedback,
  progress checks, bibliography verification, defence questions) whose findings are
  grounded in the thesis text and measured against synthetic theses with planted
  defects.
authors:
  - family-names: Czech
    given-names: Sławomir
repository-code: "https://github.com/SlawCzech/corvus-academic"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-07"
keywords:
  - thesis supervision
  - academic review
  - large language models
  - LangGraph
  - higher education
